<body>
    <h1>Albert Einstein</h1>
    <p>
        <strong>Albert Einstein</strong> was one of the most influential
        scientists of the twentieth century. He was born on
        <mark>14 March 1879</mark> in Ulm, Germany.
    </p>

    <h2>Early Life</h2>

    <p>
        Einstein showed a deep curiosity about the world from a young age.
        He was fascinated by mathematics, science, and the mysteries of the
        universe.
    </p>

    <p>
        One of his most famous ideas was the relationship between energy and
        mass, expressed by the equation <strong>E = mc<sup>2</sup></strong>.
        This equation became one of the most famous equations in physics.
    </p>

    <p>
        Einstein believed that curiosity and imagination were essential to
        learning. He famously said, <q>Imagination is more important than
        knowledge.</q>
    </p>

    <blockquote>
        "The important thing is not to stop questioning. Curiosity has its
        own reason for existing."
    </blockquote>

